WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.340 --> 00:00:09.080
Since the nuclear deal was signed back in 2015,

00:00:09.080 --> 00:00:13.580
the US Navy has seen a significant increase in the harassment

00:00:13.580 --> 00:00:16.840
from swarms of Iranian small boats in the Persian Gulf.

00:00:16.840 --> 00:00:20.660
These encounters put lives and shipping at risk.

00:00:20.660 --> 00:00:24.320
In one instance, in April 2017,

00:00:24.320 --> 00:00:26.880
the USS Mahan fired warning shots

00:00:26.880 --> 00:00:31.880
and had to make dangerous changes of course to avoid hitting one of these vessels.

00:00:31.880 --> 00:00:33.900
Why does Iran do this?

00:00:33.900 --> 00:00:36.940
While this behavior may appear to be strictly aggressive,

00:00:36.940 --> 00:00:40.000
Tehran actually has a very weak conventional navy,

00:00:40.000 --> 00:00:42.600
and it's dependent on its asymmetric,

00:00:42.600 --> 00:00:49.320
frankly guerilla-style, naval forces to deter more powerful adversaries like the US.

00:00:49.320 --> 00:00:52.540
Regardless, Washington needs to respond more firmly,

00:00:52.540 --> 00:00:56.880
and continue investing in new technologies like the Longbow Hellfire missile,

00:00:56.880 --> 00:00:59.560
which can shoot out several missiles in sequence,

00:00:59.560 --> 00:01:05.100
to ensure the safety of our personnel and freedom of navigation in the Persian Gulf.

